apy referral . hey dragon , order an autoimmune profile . and then from a hypertension standpoint you , because your blood pressure is a little elevated today , i\'d like you to continue to monitor it at home and , you know , send me a report in the next couple of weeks sh- , you know , giving me the , the blood pressure reportings . do you have a blood pressure cuff at home ?\n[patient] yes , i do .\n[doctor] okay . and then , um , we\'ll go ahead and order a lipid profile for you . hey dragon , order a lipid profile . and then for , from a diabetes standpoint let\'s go ahead and , uh , continue you on your metformin 500 mg twice a day . okay ?\n[patient] okay .\n[doctor] do you have any questions ?\n[patient] no , that\'s it .\n[doctor] okay . the nurse will be in soon . it was good to see you .\n[patient] nice seeing you too .\n[doctor] hey dragon , finalize the note .\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nLeft knee pain.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nJanet Brown is a 33-year-old female who presents today for evaluation of left knee pain.\n\nThe patient reports that she has been experiencing pain in her left knee for the past 2 weeks. The pain is bilateral and is worse with activity. She notes that she has been doing more stair workouts, which she thought was building muscle on her knees and was supposed to help. She denies any other joint pain such as elbows or shoulders, but she notes that she had a rotator cuff repair 2 years ago. She denies any pins and needles in her feet or swelling in her legs. She does note that she monitors her blood sugar levels and has diabetes. She denies fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, or shortness of breath. She has been taking Norvasc 5 mg daily and has been compliant with it. She denies that her blood pressure has elevated recently.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.\n• Musculoskeletal: Endorses bilateral knee pain.\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest